# spun.cat holds als001, and mame-alias.sh has moved @ALIAS@ to als002 in the
# database. .spun get by the alias now gets als002, which is not installed,
# so it offers als002's suggested directory; y installs it. Then .spun get of
# an alias that names no app, through gui-test.py's proxy (@PORT@), ends with
# an error. ON ERROR traps it, which keeps the autoexec running but also keeps
# BASIC from printing the report, so the screen shows "Opening" and no app
# title. The handler prints SPUNERR with the error code and the line of the
# second get (40), which shows that the get ended with an error, then waits in
# a loop. mame-alias.sh checks the proxy's log for the server's NoApp_ERROR,
# that SPUNERR names the line of the second get, and mame.log for no machine
# reset. It has no noreset: NextZXOS fetches $0000 once when a handler catches
# the error of a dot command, with BASIC at the line of that command.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
put @CAT@ /sys/spun.cat
autostart .spun get @ALIAS@
autostart ON ERROR ERROR TO e,l:PRINT "SPUNERR ";e;" ";l:FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
autostart .spun -p @PORT@ get nosuchalias
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 35
key 16 y
snap 15 20 26 34
screen 34 Alias Test B
screen 34 Install to C:/apps/alsb? (y/n) y
screen 34 SPUNERR 255 40
